// Guest ID System
// ===============
// Format: GXX-YY-ZZZ
//
// Guest IDs include information about floor, room type, and check-in date
// to help staff quickly identify guest details from the ID alone.

// ===== ID Structure =====

GXX-YY-ZZZ

// XX = Floor number (01-20)
// YY = Room type code
// ZZZ = Sequential number

// ===== Room Type Codes =====

ST - Standard
DE - Deluxe
EX - Executive
SU - Suite
PE - Penthouse
FA - Family
SI - Single
DO - Double
KI - King
QU - Queen

// ===== Example IDs =====

G03-ST-001 - Floor 3, Standard Room, 1st guest
G05-DE-012 - Floor 5, Deluxe Room, 12th guest
G10-SU-007 - Floor 10, Suite, 7th guest
G01-KI-025 - Floor 1, King Room, 25th guest

// ===== How IDs Are Made =====
// - Floor number indicates which floor the guest is staying on
// - Room type code indicates what type of room they booked
// - Sequential number is assigned per floor and room type
// - Each floor/room type combination has its own sequence

// ===== ID Number Meaning =====
// - First part (GXX): Floor number
// - Second part (YY): Room type
// - Third part (ZZZ): Sequential number for that floor and room type

// ===== Example Assignments =====
// First guest on floor 3 in a Standard room: G03-ST-001
// 50th guest on floor 5 in a Deluxe room: G05-DE-050
// 8th guest on floor 10 in a Suite: G10-SU-008

// ===== Notes =====
// - IDs are not reused for new guests
// - Each guest keeps their ID for their entire stay
// - Room changes during stay do not change the ID
// - IDs can be reused after a guest checks out
// - Helps staff quickly identify guest location and room type
// - Useful for organizing guest records by floor and room type